# Put a Ring of Elemental Command (Fire) on chargen.keys' orc barbarian, with
# mana enough to fire a wand at himself. Included by ring-fire-shards.keys and
# ring-fire-ice.keys, which differ only in which wand they then acquire and
# fire. Finding PA-08-F2 of bd inc-tek.8.8.
#
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu. Later
#                            entries are 'w' alone; the 'y' answers the
#                            one-time "enter wizard mode?" question.
#   Wizard Mode Switches     DOWN*7 walks to Infinite Mana, the 8th row
#   DOWN*7 SPACE ESC         (src/Tables.cpp:2610-2656). SPACE toggles and does
#                            not move the cursor. Without it the barbarian
#                            runs out of mana before the wand goes off.
#   Item Acquisition         RIGHT*26 walks the glyph row to Rings: ItemGlyphs
#   RIGHT*26                 (src/Tables.cpp:320) puts -AI_RING 26 steps along,
#                            and the header line names the category.
#   @until "Ring of Elemental the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#     Command (Water)" DOWN   cursor is walked. Three rows show and the MIDDLE
#                            one is selected, so the run stops on the pass
#                            where the row BELOW the wanted one appears. Water
#                            is the entry after Fire in lib/m_items.irh. The
#                            check does not trust that ordering: it reads the
#                            ring's name back off the inventory screen.
#   ENTER m SPACE ESC        take it, move the cursor to the Left Ring slot,
#                            SPACE to put it on (src/Managers.cpp:873), close.
#                            The manager refuses to close with an item in the
#                            air, so a missed SPACE cannot pass unnoticed.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7
SPACE
ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*26
@until "Ring of Elemental Command (Water)" DOWN
ENTER
m
SPACE
ESC
